      "text": "To solve the problem, we first need to determine the value of \\( n \\). The median of a set of five numbers is the third number when the set is arranged in ascending order. Given that the median is 9, we can deduce the following about the set:\n\n\\[ n, n+5, n+6, n+9, n+15 \\]\n\nThe third number in this ordered set is \\( n+6 \\). Since the median is 9, we have:\n\n\\[ n+6 = 9 \\]\n\nSolving for \\( n \\):\n\n\\[ n = 9 - 6 \\]\n\\[ n = 3 \\]\n\nNow that we have \\( n = 3 \\), we can substitute it back into the original set to get:\n\n\\[ \\{3, 8, 9, 12, 18\\} \\]\n\nNext, we calculate the mean of this set. The mean is the sum of the elements divided by the number of elements. The sum of the elements is:\n\n\\[ 3 + 8 + 9 + 12 + 18 = 40 \\]\n\nThe number of elements is 5. Therefore, the mean is:\n\n\\[ \\text{Mean} = \\frac{40}{5} = 8 \\]\n\nSo, the mean of the set is:\n\n\\[ \\boxed{8} \\]\n\nNow, let's verify this solution with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the set based on the calculated value of n\nn = 3\nnumbers = [n, n + 5, n + 6, n + 9, n + 15]\n\n# Calculate the mean of the set\nmean = sum(numbers) / len(numbers)\nprint(mean)\n```",
